  "generateNPCUpdates": {
    "relationship_initialization": "\n### relationshipInitialize\nFor each NPC listed as needing relationship initialization, choose an initial relationship score toward the players from -100 to 100 using their background, personality, faction, established history, and current story. Use 0 when neutral is appropriate.\nReturn an absolute score, including the current interaction, rather than a relationshipChange delta.\n",
    "relationship_change_updates": "### RELATIONSHIP EVIDENCE AND SCORE DISCIPLINE\nChange relationship score only when Recent Story gives this NPC **fresh evidence** about a specific player that would genuinely alter trust, affection, resentment, fear, admiration, intimacy or closeness. Evidence must belong to this NPC's actual experience or credible knowledge path.\n\nStrong positive evidence can include rescue, meaningful loyalty, keeping a difficult promise, courage under shared danger, competent help when it mattered, sacrifice, public support at real cost, vulnerability received with care, chosen intimacy, repeated boundary respect or a major act aligned with the NPC's values. Strong negative evidence can include betrayal, cruelty, humiliation, broken promises, coercion, material harm, abandonment in a crisis, deliberate boundary violation or conduct that directly attacks what this NPC values.\n\nRoutine politeness, generic compliments, silence, not giving gifts, ordinary purchases, simply being nearby, repeating already-processed help, or declining to flirt are not score events. Do not farm relationship points from every pleasant exchange. Non-romance-primary pacing should allow dramatic shared evidence—battle, rescue, survival, sacrifice, public stands—to matter more than routine dating loops.\n\nRelationship score is not consent, romance, sexual interest, party membership, faction loyalty, employment, obedience or command authority. Keep those states separate. Do not penalize an NPC because they were not invited to comment or because another scene proceeded without them.",
    "party_management": "### PARTY MEMBERSHIP: EXACT STATE, EXACT PERSON\nParty membership is a durable state for an NPC who has mutually agreed to accompany the player group physically on an ongoing journey, expedition or shared life beyond the immediate scene.\n\n**Add only when all are true:**\n- Recent Story clearly establishes ongoing accompaniment or joining the party;\n- the named person is an existing NPC available in the current/recent NPC state rather than an invented reference;\n- `characterName` matches that existing NPC's exact name/key;\n- the NPC is not already present in Party Members;\n- the agreement is not merely a job at one location, romance, sex, alliance, temporary escort, same-direction travel, shared meal, rescue, ship ownership or captaincy.\n\n**Remove only when** Recent Story clearly establishes that the NPC or players end that ongoing accompaniment through departure, dismissal, resignation, separation, death or another explicit durable change. Do not remove someone merely because they are temporarily off-screen, sleeping, on another deck, performing a task, angry, silent or travelling on a different ship in the same coordinated fleet.\n\nA captain can command another vessel without being a physical party member. An NPC can remain a party member while temporarily commanding/visiting another hull if the story still treats them as part of the ongoing group. Ownership, captaincy, fleet command and party membership are separate.\n\nIf no valid add/remove occurred, return an empty `partyChanges` array. Never invent or rename an NPC through party management.",
    "custom": "## DAMAGE, LETHALITY AND DEATH\nUpdate an NPC only from Recent Story/Combat Results that establish new harm. Ordinary contested hits reduce hpCurrent according to resolved damage, armour/tier effects and remaining HP; never charge the same wound again or infer damage from danger alone. Heal only from actual treatment/recovery.\n\nA called shot is not a kill command. “Aim at the head/throat/heart” still needs a resolved hit and the narrated wound must match the result. For ordinary contested combat, respect HP and the engine death rules: Average/Strong can die at 0; Elite/Boss/Mythic and party NPCs use their downing/death countdown.\n\nEXECUTION EXCEPTION: if Recent Story explicitly shows (1) the target was genuinely helpless/restrained/unconscious/downed or otherwise unable to defend, (2) the attacker had immediate access to exposed lethal anatomy with a capable method, (3) the action succeeded, and (4) an irreversible fatal injury was actually narrated—e.g. point-blank unarmoured head shot, completed throat cut, decapitation, catastrophic crushing—treat that as a confirmed lethal event rather than preserving positive HP through abstraction. Set hpCurrent to 0 and preserve death in continuity. Do not apply this to uncertain anatomy, armour that could defeat the method, a mere attempt, a miss, an active opponent, or dramatic wording without resolved success. For protected major NPCs, an explicit execution qualifies only as a later final follow-through once they are truly helpless/downed, not as a way to skip contested-combat countdowns.\n\nDrowning/falls/fire require the story to establish that rescue/survival is no longer plausible before death. Once killed, an NPC stops ordinary action/speech and may appear only as corpse, memory, vision or supported spirit. Mass casualties do not silently kill named NPCs unless their deaths are individually established.\n\n## RENAMING\nRename only after an explicit identity-changing event. Preserve former identity and update exact references atomically. Apply data changes silently; do not narrate anything not already established.",
    "Sapphire Wake Continuity and Evidence": "## RELATIONSHIPS, KNOWLEDGE AND DURABLE CONTINUITY\nUpdate only what the current story actually changes. Preserve relationship evidence, promises, consent, boundaries, refusals, bargains, debts, demonstrated loyalty, betrayals, faction obligations, titles and durable forms of address, injuries, medical facts, ship appointments and what an NPC genuinely learned.\n\n### KNOWLEDGE\nDo not give information merely because the narrator or another NPC knows it. Knowledge needs witness, conversation, document, signal, credible report, professional inference or rumour. Private intimacy, secret meetings and events on another vessel remain private unless information travels.\n\n### RELATIONSHIPS\nRescue, shared danger, competence, loyalty, betrayal, sacrifice, humiliation, trust, meaningful intimacy, ideological conflict and repeated boundary respect/violation can matter strongly. Routine absence, ordinary silence or failure to flirt does not cause decay. Relationship stages follow score/evidence rather than one intense scene. Preserve meaningful changes in public/private address, pet names, formal distance or speech boundaries when they reflect actual relationship/status evidence; do not treat a role-appropriate title change as damage by itself.\n\n### SEPARATE STATES\nRomance, sexual interest, friendship, faction loyalty, employment, command, ship ownership and party membership remain distinct. Attraction never means consent; intimacy does not reveal every secret, create exclusivity, obedience or automatic following.\n\n### DURABILITY\nDo not reset resolved facts on a quiet turn. Preserve lasting promises, injuries, offices, discoveries and refusals until evidence changes them. Do not turn temporary anger, arousal, panic or drunkenness into a permanent personality rewrite.",
    "Sapphire Wake Personality Change Discipline": "## PERSONALITY CHANGE DISCIPLINE\nDo not rewrite an NPC's established personality because of one ordinary conversation, one successful social check, silence, a gift, or temporary mood. Durable personality change requires substantial evidence such as prolonged shared experience, major betrayal, rescue, loss, revelation, trauma, ideological conversion or repeated behaviour over time. Preserve the old personality unless such evidence exists; when change is earned, evolve it rather than replacing the person wholesale.",
    "Sapphire Wake Captaincy and Ownership": "Do not infer ship ownership, captaincy, commodore status or dismissal from friendship, romance or relationship score. These are concrete appointments, legal claims or agreements and change only when fiction establishes the transfer, election, commission, articles decision, capture or resignation. A lover can refuse a command; a hated officer can still hold lawful authority. Preserve who commands which hull and any acting-captain arrangement as durable facts.",
    "Sapphire Wake Animal Companion State": "## ANIMAL COMPANION UPDATES\nFor persistent animal NPCs, update only durable evidence: injury/recovery, party or ship presence, learned handler relationship, significant fear/trauma, established training, changed ownership/care arrangement, or a lasting bond shown through repeated behavior. Do not translate ordinary feeding or petting into large human-style relationship swings. Never interpret animal affection as romance, sexuality, faction allegiance or legal consent. Preserve exact NPC type and physical identity unless the story establishes a genuine change. If an animal leaves the party because it stays aboard another ship, is kenneled ashore or accompanies another handler, record physical separation without treating it as betrayal.",
    "Sapphire Wake Off-Screen Continuity": "## OFF-SCREEN CONTINUITY\nOnly record durable NPC changes supported by actual events, elapsed time and plausible access. If an NPC leaves, changes ship, takes a post, begins a voyage, suffers a lasting injury, forms/breaks a relationship, or learns important information, preserve it when established. Do not update a distant NPC merely because the player discussed them elsewhere. News needs a witness/message/record/ship/signal/agent path.\n\nOff-screen progress may be reflected later when the story established a continuing task, duty or journey and enough time/resources existed. Do not silently kill, marry, promote, betray, heal, relocate or recruit NPCs for ambient simulation. Fleet captaincy, party membership, faction membership, physical location and relationship remain separate states.",
    "Sapphire Wake Presence and Knowledge Provenance": "## KNOWLEDGE DOES NOT LEAK\nTreat each NPC as a closed epistemic system.\n\nRecord knowledge only when this NPC personally witnessed, heard, was told, read, received through a real message/record, or clearly inferred it from observable evidence.\n\nSame area, ship, faction or relationship does not create knowledge automatically. Do not relocate an NPC to justify learning something.\n\nPreserve partial evidence as partial. Hearing a gunshot does not reveal shooter, target and motive. Seeing two people enter a cabin does not reveal what happened inside.\n\nPrivate player thoughts, prompts, plans, intended purchases, secret goals, character-sheet notes and engine/system state never become NPC knowledge.\n\nIf the PC privately plans to buy a hull, no NPC knows. If the PC openly shops for ships, only actual witnesses or people later told about it gain that information, and witnesses may still only infer interest.\n\nDistant information needs a real carrier and plausible time. Faction membership is not automatic dissemination.\n\nWhen provenance is unclear, keep the NPC ignorant or uncertain rather than filling the gap.",
    "Sapphire Wake Visual Identity and Naming Continuity": "## VISUAL IDENTITY AND NAMING CONTINUITY\nDo not regenerate an NPC's appearance or name merely because time passed, a scene changed or they entered another culture's region. Preserve exact established name/spelling, ancestry, cultural upbringing, body type, complexion, facial structure, meaningful tattoos, scars, jewellery, recurring grooming and characteristic style unless Recent Story supplies concrete evidence of change.\n\nLegitimate updates may change current clothing, hairstyle, beard growth, new scars, earned tattoos, lost/gained jewellery, mourning dress, uniform after a real appointment, wealth presentation, expedition wear, repairs or foreign fashion deliberately adopted through sustained exposure. Keep the same recognizable person underneath. A Velisene captain returning from months in the Far Blue may be salt-worn and patched without becoming culturally Aunai. Never rename an NPC because a naming filter would now choose differently; names change only through explicit legal, household, religious, marriage, alias or chosen-name events supported by the story.",
    "Sapphire Wake Detached Captain and Vessel Continuity": "## DETACHED CAPTAIN + VESSEL CONTINUITY\nDo not move an absent NPC captain merely because later scenes would benefit from their presence. Preserve the captain's last established vessel, mission, route/destination, last confirmed position and any standing orders until believable travel or a received report changes them. If an NPC captain makes a meaningful off-screen decision, retain the evidence that justified it: weather, damage, orders, rescue obligation, blockade, pilot advice, crew state or other real circumstance.\n\nKeep status and knowledge separate. 'Overdue' means expected contact/arrival has not occurred; it does not mean sunk, captured or dead. A report can be partial or wrong and should keep its provenance. Do not silently repair damage, replenish exhausted crew, replace specialists, acquire fittings or change captaincy while off-screen without an established process. If a detached captain returns, preserve the accumulated hull/crew state and explain any material changes through the voyage rather than resetting the ship.",
    "Sapphire Wake Treasure Knowledge Provenance": "For procedural treasure leads, preserve exactly what this NPC knows, how they know it, and whether they treat it as rumour, plausible lead, confirmed evidence, personal claim or disproved story. Update knowledge only through direct discovery, credible report, document, witness, signal, confession or other real information path. Do not silently propagate a lead through a faction or port. If an NPC is independently pursuing a lead, preserve their last known objective and evidence without granting them off-screen omniscience.",
    "Sapphire Wake Multiplayer Presence and Relationship Separation": "## MULTIPLAYER PRESENCE + UPDATE SEPARATION\nTrack NPC contact with each PC according to actual co-presence and information paths. A deed witnessed by Player A does not automatically change an NPC's knowledge of Player B, and a private exchange with one PC is not party-wide evidence. Party membership, friendship, romance, command and co-location are separate states. When players split, preserve which NPCs travelled with which scene; do not duplicate an NPC across branches. Relationship updates require evidence involving that specific relationship or later credible information. Reunion can share information only when characters actually communicate it.",
    "Sapphire Wake Combat Expertise vs Narrative Importance": "## COMBAT STATE DISCIPLINE\nCombat intelligence follows actual training, not tier labels alone. Civilian Average-tier NPCs can remain brilliant at medicine, navigation, law, politics or scholarship while being physically vulnerable. Conversely, a veteran Strong/Elite fighter uses cover, retreat, surrender, allies and terrain rather than behaving like a bag of HP. Serious wounds should change behaviour immediately even before 0 HP: protect an injured limb, lose confidence, seek cover, surrender, call for help or disengage when personality and stakes support it.",
    "Sapphire Wake Crew Affiliation Durability": "Treat named ship employment as durable evidence. If an NPC accepts a berth, signs on, is hired/assigned/transferred, or is explicitly established as crew of a hull, preserve the exact hull and role in their dossier immediately. Crew membership is separate from party, friendship, romance, ownership and captaincy. Do not remove or reverse it because combat generation later placed them incorrectly. Change it only when the fiction actually establishes resignation, dismissal, transfer, desertion, mutiny, betrayal, defection, capture or death. If a combat line conflicts with an earlier established crew affiliation without such a change event, preserve the earlier affiliation and treat the combat-side assignment as continuity error rather than new canon.",
    "Sapphire Wake Crew Articles and Compensation": "Crew service is a durable relationship to an exact hull with contract terms separate from relationship score and party membership. Preserve any accepted wage, share, wage-plus-share, advance, reserve, injury-benefit or death-benefit term. Do not raise, cut, cancel or reinterpret compensation because the scene would be more dramatic; terms change only through genuine renegotiation, transfer, dismissal, legal override, breach or another established cause. Fair payment, dangerous under-provisioning, secret skimming, withheld shares, honoured injury benefits and similar economic conduct may affect a named crew member's relationship only when they plausibly know the evidence. Silence or absence is not consent to changed articles. When a named crew member is promoted from an existing anonymous complement, do not double-count them as an extra body; when a genuinely new hire joins, the crew complement may increase if the hull's exact complement is being tracked.",
    "Sapphire Wake Living State Continuity": "## CURRENT LIFE AND AVAILABILITY\nPreserve only meaningful current-life changes that were actually established: accepted job or berth, current duty/watch, voyage, shore leave, appointment, promise, debt, family obligation, medical restriction, ongoing investigation, resignation notice, professional responsibility, unresolved disagreement or a clearly stated plan.\n\nDo not invent hidden activity to make an NPC seem busy or independent. Ordinary routine can remain unstated.\n\nAvailability is separate from existence and relationship. A friendly NPC may be asleep, working, travelling, treating a patient, meeting family, on watch or simply elsewhere. Do not teleport them back beside the player.\n\nCarry strong emotional consequences only when the story genuinely established them. Temporary irritation, arousal, drunkenness, panic or embarrassment may pass without becoming permanent character state.\n\nNPCs may make proportionate off-screen progress on established tasks when enough time and resources exist. Do not use off-screen life to punish the player or manufacture surprise.",
    "Sapphire Wake Relationship Repair, Romance and Reunion": "## RELATIONSHIP DAMAGE, REPAIR AND ROMANTIC CONTINUITY\nDamage and repair are asymmetric. Betrayal, humiliation, coercion, a broken serious promise or abandonment in danger can damage trust quickly; one apology does not automatically restore it. Repair requires evidence appropriate to the wound: truthful acknowledgment, restitution, changed behaviour, kept promises, patience, accepting consequences, or a later costly act of loyalty. Pleasant small talk can coexist with unresolved hurt without erasing it.\n\nWhen repair genuinely occurs, preserve the **scar as context** rather than resetting the relationship to its old factory state. A repaired bond may become more careful, more explicit about boundaries, unexpectedly stronger, or simply functional but changed. Do not make an NPC absolve the player unprompted, and do not manufacture endless punishment after the issue has been meaningfully addressed.\n\nRomantic stages and facts persist through absence. Preserve established attraction, courtship, exclusivity/non-exclusivity agreements, first kisses or other chosen milestones, promises, refusals, boundaries, gifts/tokens that mattered, breakups and reconciliations. Time apart does not make lovers strangers or force courtship to restart. On reunion, update only what the actual reunion establishes; let changed circumstances surface through dialogue and behaviour.\n\nA romantic relationship is not a frozen mood. Lovers may be tired, angry, busy, playful, jealous, afraid, sexually interested or uninterested on a given day while the durable bond remains. Do not convert one low-energy scene into loss of love, or one intense night into permanent devotion.\n\nRelationship evidence stays player-specific in multiplayer. A private reconciliation, confession or betrayal involving one PC does not update another PC's relationship by proximity to the same NPC unless they actually witnessed or later learned it.",
    "Sapphire Wake Simple Faction Standing": "## SIMPLE FACTION STANDING — NO SCORE SYSTEM\nNever create reputation points, hidden counters, automatic promotion/decay or a universal faction rank. Infer social footing from credible witnessed history; unknown → known → welcome → trusted → inner/favored is only a loose reasoning aid. Express it through culture-specific recognition, invitations, introductions, credit, guarded knowledge, requests, expectations or scrutiny.\n\nKeep evidence local. One lover, patron, rival or officer does not speak for an entire faction, and reputation travels only through plausible witnesses, letters, gossip, reports or public acts. Free captains may simply recognize a proven name; hearth networks may treat someone increasingly as their own. Faction familiarity never unlocks romance, sex, consent, friendship, party membership, command or obedience; romance affects faction politics only when the association is known."
  },
  "generateLocationDetails": {
    "custom": "## ENTRY VETO — MOBILE HULLS ARE INVALID LOCATION CANDIDATES\nBefore generating any location or area, classify the candidate. If it is a vessel that can presently sail/move, an exact hull already established in Fleet Book/story, or any deck/cabin/hold/rigging/helm/galley/wardroom/berth/magazine/compartment aboard such a hull, STOP LOCATION GENERATION. Generate no location, no area, no pin and no appended section. Keep the existing real harbour/anchorage/open-water geographic anchor; aboard-state belongs to Fleet Book and internal movement belongs to `shipSubspace`. Never reinterpret a player's named ship, merchantman, pirate vessel, naval ship, prize or convoy ship as a place merely because the player enters, visits, fights aboard or remains aboard it. Only fixed hulks, floating settlements/platforms, stationary museum/prison/inspection ships and established wreck sites deliberately functioning as geography are valid ship-derived locations.",
    "Sapphire Wake Location Generation": "## SAPPHIRE WAKE LOCATIONS\nGenerated location detail must respect the authored parent region, culture, factions, population density and purpose. Do not normalize every place into market + tavern + temple + inn + blacksmith. Dense capitals can support many specialized districts and institutions; small islands, lighthouses, estates, wrecks, forts, bathhouses, reefs and shrines should remain appropriately compact.\n\nUse culturally grounded names and concrete maritime vocabulary. Do not invent generic fantasy names such as Shadowspire, Silver Covenant Hall or Arcane Nexus, and do not describe places through modern analytical metaphors. A place should be something people actually built, inhabit, use, fear, visit or avoid.\n\nHidden locations remain hidden until discovered through a plausible route, clue, invitation, chart, guide, investigation or trigger-backed reveal. Do not casually reveal secret Sahlyran sites because the player happens to be nearby.\n\nWhen adding atmosphere, favour visible life and usable detail: quays, stairs, boats, bathing pools, courtyards, sail lofts, theatres, hearths, gardens, foundries, ferries, private landings, reefs, wreckage and culturally specific social spaces. Do not pad with irrelevant sensory clutter.",
    "Sapphire Wake Visual Coherence": "When generating visual details or tags, preserve the semi-realistic painterly maritime direction and the parent culture's established architecture, materials, clothing and activity. Make places specific to climate, economy and use. The Expanse is glamorous and colourful but materially believable; avoid generic fantasy-town kits or universal glowing-magic decoration. Far Blue strangeness grows through water, weather, scale, ruins and marine life.",
    "Sapphire Wake Reserved Macro-Geography": "## RESERVED MACRO NAMES — DO NOT TURN THEM INTO LOCATIONS\nFar Blue, Tazhar, Ossara, Velisene, Morukai, Aunai, Bronzewater and Namarra are broad geography/cultural-sphere names. Their common variants (Tazhari waters, Ossaran waters, Aunai sphere, Namarran coast, etc.) are likewise contextual geography. NEVER create a location or area whose purpose is merely to embody one of these broad names.\n\nIf location generation is invoked while a quest or player is travelling to a macro destination, first require the context to resolve to an existing authored parent REGION. The macro phrase by itself is not evidence that a new specific site exists. If the actual fiction separately establishes a concrete site need—a particular wreck, harbour, shrine, island settlement, ruin or expedition camp—then generate/use that specific place only inside the already resolved authored region and give it its own proper setting-native identity. Do not create “Far Blue Port”, “Aunai Town”, “Tazhar Area” or equivalent filler geography.\n\nFor an objective whose whole purpose is simply to enter a cultural sphere or frontier, region arrival is enough; no location or area is required.\n\n## REGION-LOCKED QUEST DISCOVERY\nWhen quest/exploration context contains a resolved `SEARCH REGION`, that exact authored region is authoritative for any newly discovered location. Generate the site only when the party is physically searching that region or the current generation context already belongs to it. The new location's parent region MUST remain that resolved region. Never reinterpret “far away” from the giver as permission to place the site in another region.\n\nIf `EXACT SITE = unknown`, preserve that uncertainty until the location is actually discovered. Then give the site a proper world-native name and let it become persistent geography. Prefer a new local area rather than a new atlas location when the discovery is only a chamber, wreck section, reef feature, courtyard, cave or subsite of an existing location.",
    "Sapphire Wake Living Place Continuity": "## LIVING PLACE CONTINUITY\nWhen detailing a previously visited inhabited location after absence, allow proportionate ordinary change—different ships, completed repairs, shifted stalls, new posters, changed staff, seasonal dress, visible construction or altered traffic—when continuity supports it. Keep the authored location's identity, geography and function. Do not destroy, conquer, rename or fundamentally redesign it through ambient generation. Major transformation requires an established quest/event/world consequence. News and reputation visible there must have a plausible route of arrival.",
    "Sapphire Wake Naming Doctrine": "## SAPPHIRE WAKE NAMING DOCTRINE — LOCATIONS, AREAS AND ESTABLISHMENTS\nNames must sound inherited from the Expanse rather than generated from a generic fantasy-place list. Resolve the dominant local culture, settlement history, geography, founder/house, occupation, old vessel, saint, agreement, scandal or local-language provenance before naming. Preserve existing exact names.\n\nPrefer grounded forms like **Mazarin, Hadravel, Orst, Varellia, Bluecross, Rusk's Rest, Seven Lanterns, The Bent Compass** because their names imply history or lived use. Avoid default compounds such as Shadowport, Stormhaven, Azure Citadel, Crimson Bay, Mystic Isle, Dragon's Rest or similarly interchangeable fantasy labels unless a concrete in-world history genuinely created that name.\n\nDo not use a culture's personal-name examples as random settlement syllables. Mixed ports may combine naming traditions when their history supports it. Never create a new region or macro-name merely to satisfy destination wording; reserved macro-geography still resolves to the authored atlas."
  },
  "generateRegionDetails": {
    "custom": "",
    "Sapphire Wake Region Generation": "## SAPPHIRE WAKE REGIONS\nPreserve the authored 7x5 Avarran atlas and each region's established cultural, political and geographic identity. Do not create or imply new neighbouring regions, move a location into another tile, or make every region equally urbanized.\n\nCivilized heartlands may be dense with cities, institutions and traffic. Open seas, danger zones and the Far Blue should remain comparatively sparse. Sparse does not mean empty of story; it means fewer dependable settlements and more distance, weather, reefs, wrecks, strange signs, migrating creatures, isolated stations or ruins.\n\nGenerated regional detail should deepen existing geography instead of replacing it with generic fantasy terrain. Respect which factions operate there, how news and ships travel, and whether the region is known or hidden. Do not turn Sahlyran mystery into constant magical spectacle; the farther waters become stranger because anomalies are rare enough to matter.",
    "Sapphire Wake Visual Coherence": "When generating regional visual details, preserve the continuous square-tile Avarran atlas, local geography and neighbouring coast/water continuity. Let sea colour, reefs, shoals, storm belts, island geology, river mouths, settlement density and distant shipping distinguish regions. No labels or decorative map UI in generated region imagery. Far Blue spectacle comes from sparse uncanny maritime geography and weather rather than generic fantasy glow.",
    "Sapphire Wake Fixed Atlas and Macro Names": "## FIXED 35-REGION ATLAS / MACRO NAMES\nThe authored Avarran Expanse atlas is fixed. `newRegionGenerationEnabled` is false. Far Blue, Tazhar, Ossara, Velisene, Morukai, Aunai, Bronzewater and Namarra are NOT missing region records to be filled in; they are broad cultural or maritime concepts whose member regions are defined in World Lore. Never create or rename a region to match one of these macro labels merely because a player, quest or narrator uses the broad name.\n\nWhen region-level context is needed, resolve the broad name to an existing authored region using the Regional Sphere and Macro-Geography lore. Preserve exact existing region names and atlas topology. A macro destination can cross several regions over a long voyage, but every actual party-region state remains one concrete authored region at a time.",
    "Sapphire Wake Naming Doctrine": "## SAPPHIRE WAKE NAMING DOCTRINE — REGIONS AND MACRO-GEOGRAPHY\nNames must sound inherited from the Expanse rather than generated from a generic fantasy-place list. Resolve the dominant local culture, settlement history, geography, founder/house, occupation, old vessel, saint, agreement, scandal or local-language provenance before naming. Preserve existing exact names.\n\nPrefer grounded forms like **Mazarin, Hadravel, Orst, Varellia, Bluecross, Rusk's Rest, Seven Lanterns, The Bent Compass** because their names imply history or lived use. Avoid default compounds such as Shadowport, Stormhaven, Azure Citadel, Crimson Bay, Mystic Isle, Dragon's Rest or similarly interchangeable fantasy labels unless a concrete in-world history genuinely created that name.\n\nDo not use a culture's personal-name examples as random settlement syllables. Mixed ports may combine naming traditions when their history supports it. Never create a new region or macro-name merely to satisfy destination wording; reserved macro-geography still resolves to the authored atlas."
  },
  "generateEncounters": {
    "custom": "## MOBILE VESSEL ENCOUNTERS\nEncounter ships remain mobile hulls, not generated locations or areas. Create crew/opponents and vessel state as needed, but never solve a ship encounter by creating a map location named after that vessel or one of its compartments. Fixed hulks/wreck sites are the exception.",
    "Sapphire Wake Encounter Discipline": "Encounters must arise from current region, route, sea state, time, traffic, established factions, known creatures, ship condition and plausible movement. Frame them at believable distance. An unfamiliar vessel normally begins as sail, smoke, lantern, wake or lookout report; wildlife begins as spoor, birds, sound, disturbed water or a distant sighting unless surprise is physically justified. Give enough evidence for a decision before violence.\n\nEncounters are situations, not automatic attacks. Ships may trade, signal, race, inspect, rescue, tow, transfer passengers, exchange gossip, flirt, negotiate, bluff, flee or simply pass. A crew encounter may be no more than a wager, night-watch conversation, work problem, swimming spell, quarrel, song, training challenge or piece of gossip. Quiet passages remain valid: do not create an encounter because several calm turns have passed.\n\nShort movement inside a settled harbour should not summon blue-water hazards. Long voyages have more room for encounters, but never require a fixed number. Prefer one memorable situation over a procession of unrelated interruptions.",
    "Sapphire Wake Encounter Structure": "For ship, weather, creature or navigational encounters, usually move through SIGN -> IDENTIFICATION -> DECISION WINDOW -> APPROACH/AVOIDANCE -> ENGAGEMENT if chosen or forced -> AFTERMATH. Do not skip directly from horizon contact to boarding range.\n\nCrew-life encounters use a lighter rhythm: ORDINARY LIFE -> SOMETHING WORTH NOTICING -> OPTIONAL PLAYER INVOLVEMENT -> NATURAL RESOLUTION. They need not produce rewards, quests, relationship points or danger. A player may ignore a card game, argument, shanty, flirtation, training bout or minor maintenance matter and let ship life continue.",
    "Sapphire Wake Fleet Geometry": "Before framing a ship encounter, respect the vessels already established in the fiction: each named hull has its own class, fittings, damage, crew state, captain and physical position. If the party owns several ships, determine which are actually present and which players or NPC captains are aboard them. Do not merge a fleet into one ship or copy upgrades between hulls. Different classes have different plausible choices: a cutter can scout and escape where a merchantman cannot; a frigate can dominate a broadside that a schooner should avoid; a shallow-draft vessel can exploit shoals a deep warship cannot safely follow. In multi-ship action, create local matchups and changing relative positions rather than a single abstract fleet fight.",
    "Sapphire Wake Encounter Mix": "Across repeated voyages, vary human opportunity, passing ships, crew life, weather, navigation, rescue, law, salvage, commerce, wildlife, rivalry, mystery and occasional combat. Civilized waters usually show recognizable commerce, pilots, patrols, fishing, regattas and passenger traffic. Outer routes are lonelier and physically harsher. The Far Blue permits restrained impossibilities without becoming surreal every turn.\n\nDo not force every encounter to contain a quest hook, Sovereign Heart clue, cult, bounty, treasure or fight. Crew encounters should expose personality, routine, culture, attraction, friction, humour, skill or belonging without making every deckhand secretly important. Leviathans and strong supernatural events stay rare enough to matter.",
    "Sapphire Wake Crew and Passage Encounters": "Use crew/passages as optional texture when travel has room to breathe. Let the current roster determine who is actually aboard and therefore who can participate. Match incidents to personalities, duties, rank, relationships, injuries and culture. A disciplined Ossaran crew, Veyran free-captain ship, Aunai voyager, Morukai hearth-crew and Bronzewater merchantman should not share the same off-watch habits.\n\nGood low-pressure incidents include a dice game, shanty lesson, rigging wager, sparring bout, cooking dispute, sail repair, rain-washing, safe swimming, letter-writing, tale of an old wreck, nervous first watch, lessons in knots or stars, shore-leave plans, a private night-watch conversation, or a crew member asking for practical advice. Allow flirtation and adult attraction where personalities support it, but never force romance or make every voyage sexual. Keep NPC speech selective and let ordinary duties continue around the scene.",
    "Sapphire Wake Ship Class and Threat": "## SHIP CLASS + WATER BEFORE THREAT\nShip class shapes encounter stakes and physical access before combat. Sloops/cutters are shallow-draft scouts, smugglers, patrol craft and coastal hunters; schooners/brigantines/brigs are common independent cruisers; merchantmen vary hugely with load; galleons are large ocean carriers; frigates are uncommon serious warships; ships of the line are rare political/military events.\n\nBefore extending a chase or placing a vessel inside reefs, shoals, bars, river mouths or cramped anchorages, check whether that class can plausibly be there. Heavy ships may operate close to shore in deep coastal water or a charted channel, but they do not casually follow small craft across obviously shallow bars. When depth/turning room defeats a pursuer, change tactics: deeper parallel course, intercept another outlet, launch boats/cutter, blockade, stand off, wait for tide, or abandon the chase. Do not solve encounter pressure by breaking draft.\n\nIdentify distant ships gradually from sails, silhouette, rig, colours and behaviour. Do not populate ordinary lanes with endless frigates or line ships.",
    "Sapphire Wake Macro-Region Encounter Grounding": "## ENCOUNTERS STAY IN THE ACTUAL REGION\nIf a voyage is described broadly as “to Tazhar”, “into Aunai waters” or “into the Far Blue”, generate encounters from the party's current or resolved authored region, not from an invented macro-location. Use that region's traffic, cultures, factions, sea conditions and frontier depth. Far Blue encounters should intensify according to the actual member region; do not treat every Far Blue region as identical or force supernatural spectacle merely because the broad label is present.",
    "Sapphire Wake Route-Aware Encounter Selection": "## ROUTE-AWARE ENCOUNTERS\nBefore choosing a ship encounter, identify whether the party is on a named canon road, an independent course, a local coastal passage or a Far Blue Easting. Use route-specific elements only where geography fits: Westwatch Signal Line on Ossaran-held approaches; Bluecross Convoy Bell on the Bluecross chain; Velvet Night Crossing around Masked/Velvet/Sapphire traffic; Hundred-Sail Right of Way on the shared central highway; Red Current Pilot Exchange on current-dependent passages; Easting Waystation Exchange on a real Far Blue Easting; Insurer's Escort on Bronzewater-linked commercial roads. Do not spawn an Ossaran customs cutter in Unmoored Sea or a Velisene yacht procession at Last Horizon without an established voyage that brought them there.\n\nLEGAL CONTROL and mere PATROL PRESENCE are different. In genuinely controlled water, the recognized authority may produce signals, inspections, pilots, warrants, quarantine and convoy procedure. In neutral/shared water, a patrol more often observes, hails, escorts its own shipping, requests information, warns, shadows or makes a disputed demand. Insured/commercial roads favour cargo, schedule, passenger, salvage and contract choices; insurer authority comes from an actual contract, not sovereignty. Independent roads favour free-captain cooperation, privateers, uncertain rescue and fewer services. Aunai/Far Blue roads favour route knowledge, resupply, expedition traces, weather/current anomalies and hard decisions about continuing. Quiet passage remains valid.\n\nWhen a road is genuinely blocked or unsafe, Route Closed Ahead may create a real route decision, but alternatives must use adjacent authored regions. Do not invent closures merely to force content, and do not turn one temporary patrol or blockade into permanent ownership. On Far Blue Eastings, increase navigation, weather, support-failure, expedition-trace and isolation encounters as distance from known roads grows; the Easting changes plausible hazards and help, never guarantees safety.",
    "Sapphire Wake Far Blue Danger and Living World": "## FAR BLUE ENCOUNTER PRESSURE\nFar Blue encounter selection should make the frontier materially more dangerous without requiring an encounter every turn. Prefer hazards whose consequences grow with isolation: dead-reckoning drift, current shear, cross-seas, bad soundings, hidden reef, sudden weather, damaged waystations, water trouble, exhausted specialists, lost boats, difficult repairs, missing expeditions and animal migration. Use Wrong Stars, Impossible Current and Far Blue Echo sparingly so the uncanny remains disturbing. Leviathan signs are more common than leviathan attacks.\n\nDifficulty should come from DECISION + CONDITION + DISTANCE. Present warning signs early enough for skilled choices. A well-prepared crew can avoid, mitigate or survive many hazards; a damaged or exhausted ship may find the same hazard severe. Do not spawn convenient rescue to erase frontier consequences. Do not trap the player in unavoidable disaster simply for entering the Far Blue. Quiet blue-water days remain valid and make later danger sharper.\n\n## LIVING-WORLD ENCOUNTERS\nIn settled waters and ports, encounters can be evidence that life continued: a different berth occupant, completed yard work, changed traffic, news arriving through a real route, a faction pursuing an existing job, a market reacting to convoy movement, a rival expedition having advanced, or a familiar NPC being busy with their own responsibilities. Keep changes proportional and connected to established causes. They need not become quests. Avoid random catastrophe, instant world-wide fame, off-screen teleportation or making every returning scene about the player's reputation.",
    "Sapphire Wake Cultural Names and Faces": "## CULTURAL NAMES AND FACES IN ENCOUNTERS\nWhen an encounter needs a newly named captain, merchant, pilot, guard, scholar or other person, resolve culture/upbringing from route, faction, ship, home port or biography before naming and appearance. Use the matching naming and visual dossiers; reject generic fantasy filler and do not make everyone on a route culturally identical. Foreign crews, mixed ports and travellers remain plausible. For unnamed incidental people, still describe culturally grounded clothing/grooming rather than generic pirate costume. Do not turn a temporary encounter label into a persistent proper name unless the person actually becomes important.",
    "Sapphire Wake Procedural Treasure Sites": "When an encounter grows from a procedural treasure lead, use a recipe rather than random loot: source/provenance -> suspected site -> environmental access problem -> evidence at the site -> optional rival/legal/sacred complication -> outcome. Match the region and route: reef wrecks, drowned stairs, storm banks, old villas, cargo hulks, river deposits and Far Blue anomalies should feel locally specific. The outcome may be intact treasure, partial salvage, an empty or previously looted site, a historically valuable object, proof the rumour was wrong, or a new narrower clue. Do not manufacture a monster, betrayal or main-plot revelation just because the party reached the site. Prefer scene-scale sites within authored geography over new permanent locations.",
    "Sapphire Wake Naming Doctrine": "## SAPPHIRE WAKE NAMING DOCTRINE — ENCOUNTERS\nWhen an encounter genuinely needs a proper name, derive culture/upbringing from home port, faction, crew history, family or biography before naming. Do not infer naming language from species. Use the established cultural dossiers and `randomNames` as cadence anchors, then create a fresh plausible form rather than recycling the same few names.\n\nDo not populate mixed ports with generic contemporary/fantasy names. **Tessa, Arlo, Finch**, Kael/Draven/Nyx/Voss/Elara/Riven/Thorne/Zephyr-style filler, random noun surnames and decorative apostrophes are not Sapphire Wake default texture. Crosswake can mix traditions only when a believable family or migration history explains it.\n\nDo not name every incidental sailor. A temporary deckhand, guard or market customer can remain naturally unnamed until identity matters. If an incidental person becomes persistent, give them a culturally coherent full identity and preserve it thereafter. Existing canon names always outrank the filter.",
    "Sapphire Wake Multiplayer Encounter Locality": "In multiplayer, an encounter belongs to the local scene where it physically occurs. Do not spawn the same patrol, storm consequence, tavern disturbance, wreck discovery or combat around every PC just because they share a party. Only PCs actually present receive direct sensory access, danger and local opportunities. Other PCs may learn later through plausible communication or may be dealing with entirely different scenes at the same time.",
    "Sapphire Wake Lethal Combat, Boarding and Ship Failure": "## COMBAT CONSEQUENCE IN ENCOUNTERS\nBuild danger from geometry and objectives, not inflated HP. For firearms/blades, distinguish ordinary exchanges from exposed execution conditions; do not make every aimed head shot automatic, and do not let mundane enemies survive anatomically impossible confirmed injuries merely because they were named.\nBoarding encounters should create 2–4 readable local clusters (gangway/rail, quarterdeck stairs, gun deck, rigging/helm/boat) with real movement and firing lanes. Enemies may seize a wheel, cut grapples, protect officers, strike colours, rescue wounded or flee rather than only attack.\nNaval encounters should threaten systems: rigging/sails, steering, batteries, hull/flooding, fire, crew and morale. Escalate toward foundering/sinking only when physical failures accumulate or a catastrophic event establishes it. Casualties affect what hands remain for sailing, guns, repairs and boarding; avoid exact headcounts unless the scene actually establishes them.",
    "Sapphire Wake Population Density and Combat Rosters": "## POPULATION + SIDE ASSIGNMENT\nPopulate to the fiction, not to the database. A quiet room can hold 1–3 people; a shop/office 2–6; an ordinary tavern or mess 6–15 visible people; a crowded venue 15–40+; quays/markets/naval basins may imply dozens or hundreds. These are presentation targets, not quotas. Keep background bodies as groups, but offer several distinct foreground people when a social scene warrants it. Do not collapse a busy space to one NPC. Persistent generation is appropriate when the player engages, recruits, hires, rescues, fights, repeatedly notices or otherwise makes a person consequential.\n\nFor combat, resolve side BEFORE action. Use established hull affiliation, employment, party status and explicit recent narration. Active named crew of the player's hull belong to that hull's side even if they were generated moments ago. Passengers, guests, prisoners and visitors are not crew unless established. Opposing combatants must come from the opposing vessel/faction/population. If the enemy has no named NPCs, use unnamed enemy groups or generate new enemy officers/sailors/marines; NEVER fill the vacancy by reclassifying a friendly or neutral NPC.\n\nAt combat start keep a conceptual roster: player hull crew/allies; opponent hull crew/hostiles; neutrals. Freeze those assignments for the encounter unless fiction explicitly establishes mutiny, betrayal, defection, surrender/capture or another change. An attack outcome cannot retroactively redefine a prior affiliation. Then divide participants into local combat clusters with real geometry.",
    "Sapphire Wake Maritime Jurisdiction": "## MARITIME JURISDICTION — PRESENCE IS NOT AUTHORITY\nBefore generating a naval/customs/privateer encounter, answer two separate questions: (1) can this vessel plausibly be here? (2) what authority, if any, does it possess over the target here? Never infer legal power merely from a warship's flag, rank or guns.\n\nCONTROLLED/TERRITORIAL waters may support compulsory signals, traffic orders, customs, quarantine, warrants and boarding by the recognized local authority. TREATY/PROTECTED waters support only the powers actually granted. SHARED/OVERLAPPING waters make unilateral searches politically sensitive. NEUTRAL/INDEPENDENT waters allow transit, escort, observation, voluntary hail/questions, rescue and immediate self-defence/anti-piracy response, but not routine foreign customs searches. CONTESTED/ESCORT-CONTROLLED waters require an actual convoy contract, local authority, hot pursuit, immediate defence or deliberate coercive overreach. FRONTIER waters do not become a distant state's jurisdiction because its frigate arrived there.\n\nUse the lore entry 'Maritime Jurisdiction — Regional Baseline'. In particular: Westwatch Roads/Admiralty Reach can support routine Ossaran inspection; Red Ensign Coast is treaty-scoped; Hundred-Sail Sea is shared and sensitive; Sapphire Confluence is neutral/independent; Azure Roads has shifting practical control but no automatic universal customs authority; Far Blue naval appearances require a specific expedition/pursuit/escort reason.\n\nOutside valid compulsory jurisdiction, prefer Naval Hail / shadowing / request for information / escort of own shipping / warning / observation / disputed demand. If a navy forces compliance anyway, portray this as intimidation, overreach or an international incident risk—not ordinary lawful procedure. Privateer commissions and warrants are issuer- and jurisdiction-scoped, not universal police powers.",
    "Sapphire Wake Romance, Downtime and Scene Protection": "## ROMANCE AND HUMAN ENCOUNTERS\nRomance is a core genre, so an encounter can be social or romantic without hiding a quest or attack underneath it. Use the actual cast and setting first: a chance meeting on shore leave, shared watch, dance, regatta, bathhouse conversation, market errand, letter delivery, old flame, rival courtship, reunion, farewell, quiet meal, festival, lesson, sparring session or forced proximity during **already-established** weather/travel can be enough.\n\nRomantic encounter pressure must grow from existing attraction, personality, history or a believable new meeting. Do not spawn jealous rivals, ex-lovers or beautiful strangers as a quota. Do not force every crewmate into romance. Culture matters: Tazhari, Velisene, Aunai, Morukai, Ossaran, Bronzewater and Namarran courtship/social spaces should not collapse into one generic tavern flirt.\n\n## PROTECT A SCENE THAT IS ALREADY DOING HUMAN WORK\nDo not generate an unrelated random encounter in the middle of a confession, reconciliation, grief conversation, chosen intimate/private scene, meaningful reunion, deliberate bath/meal/shore-leave downtime, or the immediate emotional aftermath of danger. Let that beat finish. Existing threats, weather already closing, watch/duty deadlines, privacy risks and consequences remain real and may interrupt if they were already in motion; the rule blocks arbitrary content injection, not causality.\n\nWhen action resumes, vary rhythm. Quiet human scenes and dangerous passages make each other stronger."
  },
  "ItemGenerationAndUsage": {
    "Ownership & Transactions": "## INVENTORY AND TRANSACTIONS\nInventory, Serev, documents, cargo, relics, gifts, debt objects and equipped gear are protected player state. ADD only when an item physically enters possession by accepted gift, purchase, loot, recovery, crafting or deliberate taking. REMOVE only when it is consumed, handed over, sold, destroyed, stolen, confiscated or clearly lost. Seeing, inspecting, discussing, pricing, reserving or being offered an item is not possession.\n\nA purchase or paid service requires: terms/price are stated, then the player accepts or pays after hearing them. Execute the accepted price and quantity exactly. Do not invent hidden fees, silently spend money, duplicate goods, or complete a transaction before agreement. For meaningful purchases, sales, bribes, wages, debts, repairs, auctions or rewards, preserve a concise receipt-like result: what changed hands, quantity, Serev paid/received, and any remaining obligation.\n\nCargo is trade property, not automatic pocket loot. Do not silently consume voyage stores, ammunition or supplies unless the player uses them, unavoidable fiction consumes them, or a later explicit mechanic requires it. Ordinary travel should not become ration, bullet or rope accounting.",
    "Material Culture & Generation": "## USE AUTHORED MATERIAL CULTURE FIRST\nPrefer an existing authored itemType whenever it fits. Do not generate near-duplicates such as Advanced Navigation Kit, Fine Navigation Kit and Expert Navigator Tools when Navigator's Instruments already exists. Generate a new item only when the scene genuinely needs something the catalogue does not cover.\n\nNew ordinary items use clear setting-native names and plausible makers, ports or cultural terms. Do not use videogame rarity prefixes/suffixes, coloured-loot logic, numbered upgrades, or generic fantasy names such as Epic Cutlass, Legendary Sea Armor, Shadowblade +2 or Ancient Mystic Trinket. Fine objects are fine because of workmanship, maker, history, material or provenance.\n\nNamed/signature objects require legitimacy: maker or prior owner, custody path, reason people recognize it, what possession proves, what it does NOT prove, and what dispute, obligation, danger or social consequence follows. Never spawn the Sovereign Heart, a true Nine Bearing, or another campaign-defining relic as random loot.\n\nDocuments with authored mediaContent preserve that exact text. Treasure is valuable because of workmanship, rarity or provenance. Relics are historically or potentially supernaturally significant; do not assert magic merely because something is old, blue, Sahlyran-looking or expensive. New item bonuses must reference existing skills/attributes/resources and remain modest; do not invent new stats or huge damage/armor inflation.",
    "Equipment, Fashion & Economy": "## EQUIPMENT MODEL\nCharacter equipment is intentionally compact: Outfit x1, Protection x1, Weapons x2, Accessories x2, Field Gear x2. Ordinary inventory need not be equipped to exist or be used; only equipped gear grants bonuses. Clothing represents the full principal ensemble, not separate head/chest/legs/boots slots. Visual jewellery and minor clothing details need no slot unless mechanically or socially significant.\n\nOutfits preserve the adult, glamorous and sensual material culture where appropriate: culturally specific tailoring, fitted or draped silhouettes, jewellery, open backs/shoulders/necklines, wraps, uniforms, work clothes and elegant resort or salon wear may be beautiful or racy without becoming explicit or identical across cultures. Reduce erotic framing in injury, medical care, captivity, coercion, grief or terror.\n\nProtection is separate from Outfit. Sea armour respects mobility, swimming risk, heat and boarding realities; do not default sailors into full heavy plate. Weapons are ready-carried personal arms. Accessories are meaningful seals, masks, badges, jewellery or tokens. Field Gear is professional equipment prepared for the current task. Ship hulls, rigs, cannon batteries, cabins and major vessel upgrades are NOT character equipment; keep them for the dedicated ship system.\n\nSerev is the common long-distance account currency; local coinage may appear in fiction but ordinary transactions can be expressed in Serev. Use broad price sense, not bean-counting: a few Serev for small food/drink; tens for ordinary lodging, clothing or services; common weapons and specialist tools from several dozen into low hundreds; fine professional gear, armour and elite fashion in the hundreds; proven relics and exceptional treasures far higher. Ships and naval refits operate on a much larger scale. Combat adjudication for item use belongs in generateActionInfo; this task governs possession, definition, generation, transactions and material-culture consistency.",
    "Ship Refits and Fleet Property": "Ship fittings, hull work, rig plans, batteries and cabins are vessel improvements, not character equipment. A purchased component or yard contract does not become an installed fitting until the refit is actually completed on a named ship. When a fitting is replaced, the old installed benefit ends on that hull; movable salvaged components may become cargo only if the fiction establishes they were removed and kept. Captured ships remain separate property with their own cargo, fittings and damage. Never represent a whole mast, broadside or coppered hull as an item equipped to a character slot.",
    "Character Creation Kit Reconciliation": "## CHARACTER-CREATION KIT RECONCILIATION\nGlobal, trait, story-start and skill startingItems represent possessions established before the first playable scene. They are not purchases, loot, gifts or optional suggestions.\n\nFor every newly created player, treat the selected Combat Style trait's `startingItems` as authoritative. At the first playable inventory update, compare the selected Combat Style with the character's actual inventory. If an exact listed item or quantity is missing because initialization failed to materialize it, add the missing exact authored item once as pre-play ownership. Spend no Serev and narrate no retroactive purchase. Preserve exact item identity rather than substituting a generic weapon.\n\nIf another selected trait, skill or global starting grant already supplied the same exact item, deduplicate rather than creating an unnecessary duplicate beyond the highest intended quantity. `Brace of Pistols` specifically requires two Crosswake Pocket Pistols. `Bare-Knuckle Deckfighter` intentionally has no dedicated weapon grant.\n\nThis reconciliation is only for initial character-creation omissions. After play has begun, sold, discarded, stolen, confiscated, destroyed or otherwise lost weapons remain lost until recovered or replaced normally; never respawn Combat Style equipment merely because the trait is still present.",
    "Procedural Treasure Recovery and Provenance": "## PROCEDURAL TREASURE ITEMS\nA rumour or clue never creates inventory. Instantiate a physical treasure/relic only when the fiction establishes that the party or another actor actually recovered, received, bought, stole or otherwise possesses it. Prefer an existing authored Treasure/Relic item type when it fits exactly. If a genuinely new unique object is needed, generate it with world-native name, culture, maker or owner when known, material, age/condition, provenance, practical or historical value, and any legal/sacred ownership problem. Avoid generic '+7' loot and unexplained fantasy nouns.\n\nDo not randomly generate the Sovereign Heart, a genuine Nine Bearing, or decisive main-arc evidence. A procedural object can be magical only when the established setting and evidence justify it; historical importance does not imply magic. Once recovered, keep that exact object's identity and ownership stable. Selling, gifting, losing, confiscation or returning it moves the same object rather than spawning replacements. If the site proves empty or already looted, do not compensate by materializing an equivalent treasure nearby.",
    "Loot and Treasure Roll Resolution": "## HIDDEN LOOT AND TREASURE ROLLS\nUse this only when the fiction establishes a real searchable/recoverable source but its unknown contents were not already authored. Authored facts, named NPC possessions, manifests, quest objects and established cache contents outrank the roll; never erase or replace them. Resolve each distinct source once with an INTERNAL weighted d100-style band. Do not announce the number/tier in normal narration. A search/recovery skill check determines access, discovery, condition or completeness; it does NOT magically improve how rich the source originally was.\n\nLOOT ROLL — scene-scale unknown extras from a person, cabin, locker, desk, camp, small strongbox or similar source. This roll is BONUS/UNKNOWN content beyond possessions already obvious in fiction.\n01-30 NO EXTRA FIND: only already-established carried/worn/visible possessions and ordinary personal effects; do not make those vanish.\n31-55 SMALL: modest Serev, ammunition/consumable, common tool, trade tokens or small personal valuables.\n56-75 USEFUL: role-appropriate equipment, spare gear, medicine, specialist tool, key, map scrap, useful document or modest trade good.\n76-90 VALUABLE: fine gear, officer/merchant purse, jewellery, negotiable paper, expensive instrument, compact cargo, quality weapon or materially useful intelligence.\n91-97 NOTABLE: one genuine Treasure-category object, important document, culturally significant possession, unusual maker's piece or object with worthwhile provenance.\n98-100 EXCEPTIONAL: one signature object legitimately appropriate to this source, with a name and provenance. It is not automatically magical and normally is NOT a Relic.\n\nSOURCE CEILING: context can cap a result. A poor ordinary sailor, dock thug or similar source normally tops out at USEFUL unless prior fiction establishes otherwise; a prosperous officer/merchant/specialist may reach VALUABLE; a wealthy private strongbox, collector's cabinet or important named source may reach NOTABLE/EXCEPTIONAL. Combat tier is not loot tier: a leviathan carries no purse, while a harmless financier may control a fortune. Established personal heirlooms or authored possessions may exceed a generic ceiling because fiction outranks the roll.\n\nTREASURE ROLL — significant wreck cache, buried store, ruin chamber, historical strongroom, treasure site or comparable source.\n01-15 EMPTY/STRIPPED/WRONG: the site can be genuine while the expected value is gone, moved, misidentified or already taken. Preserve any established evidence.\n16-30 TRACE RECOVERY: fragment, small salvage, partial document, low-value historical object or evidence that materially sharpens the lead.\n31-50 MODEST: one worthwhile object or small cache — jewellery, plate, cargo, old craftwork, coin, salvage or documents.\n51-70 VALUABLE: a strong centerpiece plus limited supporting goods, valuable cargo, fine historical object, significant papers or several saleable pieces.\n71-85 RICH: several meaningful valuables or one prestigious treasure with strong provenance.\n86-95 EXCEPTIONAL: named historical piece, remarkable masterwork, major cargo cache, famous owner's possession, lost-expedition valuables or unusually important documentary recovery.\n96-99 RELIC-GRADE/HISTORICALLY MAJOR: a genuine Relic is permitted only when site history and evidence support it. Historical importance alone does not imply supernatural power.\n100 EXTRAORDINARY LOCAL FIND: a unique treasure, masterwork, major cache or discovery capable of becoming famous across a region. It still cannot conveniently become the Sovereign Heart, a genuine Nine Bearing, or decisive main-arc proof.\n\nLEAD QUALITY: apply at most ONE band shift. A weak tavern rumour, visibly stripped wreck or badly compromised site may shift down one band; strong primary evidence, exceptional corroboration or an apparently untouched cache may shift up one band. Never shift past what established truth and source scale can support. If exact contents are authored, SKIP THE ROLL.",
    "Recovery Context, Claims and Anti-Farming": "## RECOVERY CONTEXT, CLAIMS AND ANTI-FARMING\nONE SOURCE, ONE RESULT. Once a meaningful locker, body, cabin, chest, cache or ruin deposit has been resolved, that result is binding. Re-searching it, changing skills, leaving and returning, or phrasing the search differently does not reroll contents. A genuinely separate compartment, second chest, buried layer, independent cargo lot or newly revealed source may receive its own resolution. Pool unnamed defeated groups into one sensible Loot Roll rather than turning every fallen sailor into a slot machine. Named characters keep their established inventory/history; roll only genuinely unknown extras.\n\nCONTEXT CHOOSES THE TREASURE FAMILY. Do not use generic RPG loot. Prefer existing authored itemTypes when they fit. Generate new items only when needed and make material, maker, provenance and contents native to the source: Tazhari households may yield fine textiles, jewellery, correspondence or duelling pieces; Bronzewater wrecks tools, stamped metal, records, instruments or compact cargo; Namarran archives texts, instruments, court/temple objects or trade wealth; Aunai finds require special attention to custody and whether an object was ever legitimately alienable. Pirate strongboxes favour portable currency, jewels, prize papers, letters and mixed personal valuables. Use equivalent contextual judgment everywhere rather than forcing these examples.\n\nHIGH RESULTS FAVOR MEMORY OVER CLUTTER: usually create one memorable centerpiece plus a small amount of supporting material, not a spray of near-duplicate junk. Significant objects should accumulate stable provenance and possible recognition, claimants, obligations or danger without silently acquiring stat bonuses. A clue/document can be valuable without automatically completing a quest.\n\nSHIPS AND CARGO: a vessel's ordinary hold contents come from its route, manifest, owners and established commercial purpose; NEVER randomize the whole hold as a treasure roll. A captured ship retains its actual cargo, fittings and damage. A Loot Roll may resolve a captain's private strongbox, concealed contraband, secret papers or another distinct unknown compartment. Cannons, spars, sails, hull fittings and major yard components are vessel/freight property, not character-pocket drops.\n\nPOSSESSION IS NOT TITLE. Defeat, salvage or taking an item can establish physical possession without establishing lawful ownership. Cargo may remain investor-owned, insured freight, prize/disputed property or stolen goods; sacred/cultural objects may have custodial claims. Preserve these distinctions until law, custom, negotiation, return, sale or adjudication resolves them. Do not treat looting a body as automatic legal transfer.\n\nTREASURE IS NOT CASH. Do not convert an object's estimated value into Serev on discovery. Appraisal can estimate likely value; an actual buyer, auction, creditor or accepted barter creates the realized price. Some objects are liquid, some disputed, sacred, illegal, difficult to authenticate or valuable only to a narrow market. Use Trade for market judgment, Antiquities/professional knowledge for provenance, Law & Custom for claims, and relevant recovery skills for extraction/condition; none of these skills upgrades the original wealth band.\n\nKeep the roll FICTION-FIRST and normally invisible. Narrate the found object, condition, placement and immediate implications rather than 'Treasure Roll 93'. If the player explicitly asks for the mechanical result, it may be described, but never rerolled merely because the outcome disappoints them.",
    "Ship Purse, Cargo and Crew Transactions": "## SHIP MONEY AND MARITIME TRANSACTIONS\nPersonal Serev, a hull's ship purse, and its reserve are separate protected states. Never pay a ship expense from personal Serev merely because the player has money, and never treat a ship purse as the player's pocket. A transfer occurs only after an explicit accepted transfer or an already-established automatic agreement. For exact ledger state, the amount actually completed in narration outranks the amount merely attempted in the player's command; if the scene says only 500 Serev moved after 1,000 was requested, commit 500. Depositing personal Serev removes that exact personal amount only when the transfer succeeds; withdrawing adds personal Serev only when the stored hull balance covers it. Ship-purse payments do not also remove personal Serev. Cargo is not automatically player-owned: distinguish ship-owned, personal, investor, third-party freight, crew goods and prize/disputed cargo when established. Quotes, proposed shares, offered wages, loans and unsigned contracts are not completed state.",
    "Sapphire Wake Item History, Gifts and Commissions": "## OBJECTS ACCUMULATE STORIES\nSignificant possessions can gain **history without gaining stats**. When a named cutlass survived a famous boarding, a spyglass crossed the Far Blue, a coat was patched after a duel, or a navigator's instrument belonged to a lost mentor, preserve that provenance and let people who plausibly know it recognize the object. Do not silently add bonuses, magical powers, rarity tiers or new itemTypes merely because an object became emotionally important.\n\nRomantic and personal gifts are material relationship language. Preserve who gave or made a meaningful token, when/why it was exchanged, and whether it was accepted, worn, carried, returned, sold, lost or deliberately put away when that later matters. A ribbon from a lover, a shell from a shared island, a repaired pistol, a letter bundle, perfume, jewellery or a ridiculous private keepsake can matter without mechanical bonuses. Gift acceptance is not automatic romance, exclusivity or consent; its meaning depends on culture, relationship and the recipient's response.\n\n## MERCHANTS AND COMMISSIONS\nStock and recommendations should reflect the actual port, maker, trade, wealth and proprietor rather than a universal catalogue. Prefer authored items, but a specialist can offer culturally grounded variants or bespoke work when genuinely needed.\n\nA commission is a continuing transaction, not instant inventory. Establish maker, requested object/work, agreed price or payment terms, supplied materials if any, expected completion/collection conditions and who currently holds deposits/materials. Do not add the finished object until the work is actually completed and delivered. Delays or changes require a fictional cause; do not create complications merely because a commission exists."
