  "summarization": {
    "custom": "",
    "Sapphire Wake Continuity Memory": "## REMEMBER WHAT MAKES CONTINUITY HONEST\nPreserve durable facts that will change later play: current location and plausible travel; named NPC whereabouts when known; ship ownership, name, major damage and unfinished repairs; active voyages and destinations; Sovereign Heart/Bearing clues and who knows them; discovered hidden locations; faction bargains and witnessed deeds; titles, commissions, captaincy and jurisdiction; promises, debts, payments, blackmail, threats and conditions; relationship evidence, consent, boundaries and unresolved emotional consequences; injuries and lasting medical facts; open conversations and who owes the next move.\n\nFor unfinished fights, preserve practical geometry: range, local clusters, who is grappling or pinned, weapons lost or in hand, cover, blocked routes, injuries, morale and the immediate objective. For recurring rivals, preserve only what they actually witnessed or learned and what adaptation follows from that evidence.\n\nNews and secrets need information paths. Record who witnessed, heard, read or was told something when that distinction matters. Do not upgrade one faction member's knowledge into faction-wide omniscience.\n\nDo not promote decorative room trivia into memory. During romance or intimacy, remember consent, promises, boundaries, privacy, emotional aftermath and meaningful gestures—not random animals, dripping water, chores, weather or household clutter.",
    "Sapphire Wake Fleet Memory": "## FLEET + HULL IDENTITY MEMORY\nPreserve one record per physical hull: immutable Fleet Book identity/Hull # when relevant, current display name, former-name aliases, class or class-undetermined, owner, captain/acting captain, fleet-command membership, flagship status, current/last-confirmed region and location, major fittings, unresolved damage, crew condition, mission, and which PCs are actually aboard. Two hulls may share a name; never merge them. Renaming changes only the display name/aliases, not crew, purse, cargo, fittings, damage or history. Sailing updates only the exact moving hull and never copies another split player's native party-map position.\n\nFor detached vessels preserve origin/last confirmed position, destination/task, named road/Easting or region chain, next intended region, voyage stage, standing orders, rendezvous, last contact and player-knowledge status. Game ticks are change-log markers, not travel time. Separate true possibility from party knowledge; overdue is not sunk and planned rendezvous is not reunion.",
    "Sapphire Wake Campaign Memory": "Preserve active/finished authored arc consequences compactly: confirmed Bearings and their provenance; who knows each clue; regional arc outcomes; quest refusals or abandoned promises that still matter; narrative events completed or suspended; rival-expedition advantages earned through real evidence; Calyra Veyassa's chosen future; Ossaran command-crisis settlement; Bellacera chamber custody; Morukai hearth custody; Bronzewater hull ownership; First Sky publication policy; Vaelau/Aroavai route terms; Crosswake fleet-articles outcome; and each premade player's unresolved personal quest facts. Do not convert quest-log wording into omniscient NPC knowledge.",
    "Sapphire Wake Voyage Memory": "For an unfinished voyage, preserve destination, route or intended bearing, current sea/region, approximate stage of passage, relevant weather/current, important ship damage, crew strain, detached vessels, unresolved encounter contacts and any meaningful shipboard conversation or promise that should carry forward. Do not preserve every meal, card game, song or weather description. Remember ordinary crew-life incidents only when they changed a relationship, duty, injury, dispute, secret, promise, command arrangement or later choice.",
    "Sapphire Wake Ship Class Memory": "When a specific ship matters, preserve its exact name, current practical class (or class undetermined), ownership, captain/acting captain, current region/location, major fittings, lasting damage and whether it is active, detached, captured, sold or lost. Never let summarization promote a vessel to a heavier class, merge two hulls, transfer fittings between ships or treat a player's current ship as the whole fleet.",
    "Sapphire Wake Animal Companion Memory": "Preserve recurring animal companions when relevant: exact name and NPC type, current ship/location and handler, injuries, distinctive appearance, important training, fears, bonds, and unresolved separation. Do not waste summary space on every background animal. Never silently promote mimicry into speech, ordinary animal cleverness into human intelligence, or a companion's absence from a scene into relationship damage.",
    "Sapphire Wake Macro-Geography Memory": "## MACRO-GEOGRAPHY + QUEST SEARCH MEMORY\nKeep broad intention separate from exact geography: `MACRO GOAL = Far Blue; SEARCH REGION = Drowned Meridian; EXACT SITE = unknown.` Macro labels (Far Blue, Tazhar, Ossara, Velisene, Morukai, Aunai, Bronzewater, Namarra) never replace authored regions.\n\nFor exploration quests, preserve the resolved SEARCH REGION even before a site exists. Do not invent a name early or relocate the search because another region is distant. After discovery, update to `DISCOVERED SITE = <exact name>; REGION = <same resolved region>` and retain route/current/next region as relevant. Temporary unnamed landfalls keep their Wilderness-backed anchor instead of becoming fabricated permanent locations.",
    "Sapphire Wake Canon Route Memory": "## CANON ROUTE MEMORY\nPreserve the exact voyage goal, current authored region, named road/Easting when one is being used, next intended region, important diversion, and why that course was chosen when it remains relevant. Keep broad destination separate from exact route: 'Far Blue expedition via Meridian Easting; currently Drowned Meridian' is better than 'went to Far Blue.' Remember active blockades, quarantines, dangerous seasonal conditions, escort/convoy commitments, pilot agreements and route closures only while established. Do not silently promote a temporary patrol or privateer presence into permanent route ownership. Preserve whether the party deliberately chose an independent road or a serviced/controlled one.",
    "Sapphire Wake Living World and Far Blue Memory": "## LIVING WORLD + FAR BLUE MEMORY\nPreserve established changes that will matter on return: NPC relocations or continuing duties, ships departed/arrived, repairs or projects completed, active blockades/closures, changed faction activity, credible public rumours, warrants, market disruptions and other consequences with an actual cause. Preserve how important news travelled when that limits who can know it. Do not store every background change, meal, berth turnover or passerby.\n\nFor Far Blue voyages preserve current Easting/region, next intended region or retreat point, accumulated hull/rig/steering damage, crew exhaustion, injured essential specialists, water/support concerns when meaningful, lost boats or equipment, weather/current uncertainty, last trustworthy navigation evidence and distance from credible help. If the captain deliberately turned back or changed Easting, preserve WHY. Never summarize a dangerous unresolved frontier situation into 'sailing normally.'",
    "Sapphire Wake Perception and Information Provenance Memory": "## CLOSED EPISTEMIC MEMORY\nRemember who actually knows each important fact.\n\nA character knows only what they personally witnessed, heard, were told, read, received through a real message or record, or clearly inferred from observable evidence. Assume ignorance unless informed.\n\nDo not let global summary text become universal NPC knowledge. Private thoughts, unspoken plans, future purchases, hidden objectives, system state and narrator-only truth stay private until revealed in-story.\n\nKeep partial evidence partial. A sound, glimpse, rumour or suspicion does not become a complete event.\n\nSame room, ship, harbour, faction or party does not automatically merge knowledge. Preserve who was actually present and listening when it matters.\n\nDistant information needs a carrier and time. If no path exists, absent NPCs remain ignorant.\n\nRemember movement honestly. Do not relocate a person in memory because a later scene would benefit from their presence.",
    "Sapphire Wake Cultural Identity and Exact Names": "## CULTURAL IDENTITY, VOICE AND EXACT NAMES\nPreserve exact names and keep upbringing distinct from ancestry and current location. Retain durable visual anchors and genuine later changes without rewriting original identity. For recurring NPCs, also preserve speaking traits that matter to continuity: established public/private forms of address, pet names, occupational diction, speech taboos, and major shifts in respect, intimacy or status. Foreign residence, clothing or a borrowed phrase is not automatic cultural assimilation.",
    "Sapphire Wake Procedural Treasure Lead Memory": "Preserve unresolved procedural treasure hunts as compact structured continuity, using the internal TL-# identifier when one has been assigned: alleged treasure/object; original source and information provenance; current reliability; suspected region/route/location at the level actually established; confirmed evidence; contradictions or disproved claims; current best next lead; known rivals/claimants; legal or sacred ownership issues; whether the player merely heard it or actively committed; associated generated quest ID if any; and current status (rumour / corroborated / narrowed / site found / recovered / disproved / already looted / abandoned). Distinguish player knowledge from hidden truth. Never upgrade rumour into fact during summarization. Keep at most eight unresolved procedural leads in detailed memory; resolved or abandoned leads can collapse to one short historical line unless consequences remain active. Never merge procedural TL leads into Sovereign Heart/Nine Bearings clues without an authored connection.",
    "Sapphire Wake Mobile Ship Position Memory": "## MOBILE SHIP + TEMPORARY ANCHOR MEMORY\nPreserve each relevant character's exact hull separately from geography. For active ships retain hull name, current/last-confirmed region, route/geographic anchor, and shipboard subspace when needed. Never summarize a mobile vessel into an atlas location/area. Docked ships may share a harbour anchor while remaining separate from people ashore; underway fleet position overrides stale co-presence. Fixed hulks/platforms and wreck sites may remain authored locations.\n\nIf an unnamed cove, beach, reef, sandbar, islet, shoal or mooring is reached and native state represents it as `Wilderness`, preserve **TEMPORARY ANCHOR** = site description + authored region + last resolved `currentCoordinates` + exact hull + anchored/ashore state. Keep those coordinates stable until explicit departure or another true destination resolves; boat↔shore movement and local exploration do not create a new anchor.\n\nIf Captain's Cabin, Quarterdeck, Gun Deck, Hold, Rigging, Galley, Crew Quarters or similar appears aboard a mobile hull, store it only as `shipSubspace`, never geographic canon.",
    "Sapphire Wake Multiplayer Player Scene Ledger": "## PLAYER SCENE LEDGER\nFor every active PC, preserve a compact independent scene record whenever the party is split: exact/last-established region and fixed location/area, or exact hull plus useful shipboard subspace; nearby named NPCs/other PCs when relevant; immediate activity or unresolved local danger; meaningful local time offset; and the last action/decision still awaiting consequence. Do not overwrite Player B's position because Player A moved through the engine's party-level map state.\n\nPreserve private knowledge by owner. Record which PC personally witnessed, read, heard, was told or inferred an important clue, secret, bargain, crime, relationship fact or treasure lead. Do not compress this into 'the party knows' until the information was actually shared. Likewise preserve private promises, debts, arrests, wounds and scene-specific commitments when they can matter later.\n\nWhen PCs reunite, merge only physical scene topology: they are now co-present. Do not automatically merge memories or secrets. If split scenes have consumed different amounts of fictional time, retain that mismatch until the story plausibly synchronizes them. Fleet Book exact-hull presence remains authoritative for PCs aboard ships; a stale native party location never teleports another PC.",
    "Sapphire Wake Combat Geometry, Wounds and Ship Casualty Memory": "## COMBAT CONTINUITY MEMORY\nWhen a fight remains unresolved, preserve only decision-relevant geometry: each active local cluster, who is engaged with whom, range/deck/subspace, cover or blocked routes, grapples/pins, dropped/lost weapons, serious new wounds, incapacitated/dead combatants, morale/surrender state and immediate objectives. Do not collapse separate boarding clusters or split-player fights into one melee.\nPreserve established lethal facts exactly. A called-shot attempt is not a confirmed wound; a confirmed execution/fatal injury stays fatal. Do not resurrect someone because HP/state wording was later omitted.\nFor tracked ships preserve exact hull and active damage/crew states: sail/rig/spar/mast, steering, battery/guns, hull breach/flooding/foundering, fire/magazine, and casualty severity. Remember whether damage control is temporary or actually repaired. If a vessel sinks/is destroyed, record it as lost and do not silently return it or transfer its fittings to another hull.",
    "Sapphire Wake Named Crew and Allegiance Memory": "For every relevant tracked hull, preserve named crew separately from party membership: NPC exact name, exact hull, shipboard role if known, and status such as active, ashore-on-leave, wounded, captured, transferred, deserted/mutinous or dead. Recent explicit recruitment/assignment counts even if the NPC was generated in that same scene. Preserve passengers/visitors/prisoners as distinct from crew when relevant.\n\nIn unresolved combat, preserve which side each named participant belongs to and the evidence for that side. A crew member remains aligned with their hull unless an explicit change event occurred. Never summarize an accidental enemy assignment as a betrayal. If opponent NPCs were unnamed, keep them as opponent groups rather than borrowing friendly named crew. Fleet Book namedCrew state is authoritative unless later fiction explicitly changes it.",
    "Sapphire Wake Captain Ledger and Crew Economy Memory": "Preserve per-hull economic continuity: crew-articles model and custom terms; named crew compensation that differs from defaults; exact ship purse/reserve balances when established; important debts, contracts, freight/cargo ownership, unpaid obligations and last settlement; and each player's designated command hull. Keep personal Serev separate from ship money and preserve the completed amount over a merely attempted amount. Preserve Fleet Book Hull #/aliases where duplicate or renamed vessels need disambiguation. Fleet size counts active hulls under legitimate ownership/captaincy/acting-captaincy or formal fleet command, not every tracked ship. Single-player automatic Captain's Ledger is one deferred compact closeout for the player's current tracked vessel, including ordinary crew serving under an NPC captain; the operational HUD is the same and grants no command, ownership or privileged in-fiction knowledge by itself. Multiplayer players act in one shared turn: emit only ONE deferred shared closeout covering tracked vessels occupied by players plus legitimately player-authorized fleet hulls, grouped by Hull #, with a fleet-activity summary counting distinct player-occupied hulls (not falsely calling ordinary crew vessels command hulls) and at most three material hull/change lines; never stack per-player automatic ledgers or expose private purse/reserve/contracts in the shared block. Expanded fleet listings are request-only. Keep per-player designated hull and ledger-mode continuity.",
    "Sapphire Wake Maritime Jurisdiction Memory": "When a naval/customs/privateer demand matters later, preserve the asserted basis of authority: current region/water, issuer, treaty/port/convoy/warrant/hot-pursuit/emergency basis if any, whether the target accepted voluntarily, disputed it, or was coerced, and any witnessed overreach or diplomatic consequence. Do not summarize one patrol's temporary presence into permanent sovereignty, and do not turn a foreign flag into universal search/arrest authority.",
    "Sapphire Wake NPC Current Life Memory": "## NPC CURRENT LIFE MEMORY\nPreserve only current-life facts whose loss would create continuity errors: present job/berth or command, current duty when scene-relevant, ongoing voyage/destination, accepted appointment or promise, family/work obligation, medical restriction, meaningful current availability, unresolved disagreement, and a deliberate next intention that the NPC actually stated or acted toward.\n\nDo not invent an “active pressure”, hidden agenda or off-screen drama simply to make the NPC feel alive.\n\nPreserve major emotional aftermath when it truly matters, but do not store every passing mood, joke, meal, watch rotation, irritation or flirtation.\n\nKeep relationship, employment, party membership, command, attraction, consent and availability separate.\n\nIf a state ends, replace it rather than accumulating contradictory snapshots.",
    "Sapphire Wake Hard State and Generated Cast Memory": "## HARD STATE, GENERATED CAST AND REFERENCE MEMORY\n**Feelings may compress; ledgers and custody do not.** Preserve exact established balances when relevant, debts, agreed prices still outstanding, contracts/articles, commissions, promises, deadlines, item custody, confiscated/borrowed/stolen property and recovery paths, ship ownership/captaincy and durable damage. Never let summarization silently spend, restore, transfer, forgive, finish or lose hard state.\n\nGenerated recurring people are as continuous as authored ones. Preserve a named generated NPC likely to recur: exact name, established adult gender/identity, ancestry/culture, role, last plausible location/ship, enough appearance/voice to render the same person, important relationship evidence, current obligation/goal and meaningful ties. If space is tight, compress history rather than replace them.\n\nPreserve unambiguous play aliases—nicknames, shortened names and stable role references such as “the Four Flags innkeeper” or “our surgeon”—only when context established the exact referent. Never turn an established referent into a newly generated NPC. If a role later becomes ambiguous, keep the exact identity and stop relying on the alias."
  },
  "generateLearnedAbilities": {
    "custom": "",
    "Sapphire Wake Ability Learning": "## LEARNING TECHNIQUES\nPrefer the authored ability catalogue. Nonmagical abilities are learnable techniques, not class-locked powers: once a character has enough relevant skill, a plausible teacher, practice, repeated field use or a convincing story breakthrough can teach them even if their starting Calling, Combat Style or faction was different. Treat skill requirements as broad readiness gates, not reasons to deny sensible cross-training. A sailor may learn pistol work; a courtier may learn to fence; a marine may learn navigation.\n\nTrait-granted abilities are deliberately curated starting familiarity and may sit slightly above the character’s raw starting skill. Do not remove them for that small gap, but do not use trait grants to smuggle veteran or master techniques into character creation. Avoid duplicate abilities that merely rename an ordinary skill action.\n\n## COMBAT STYLE PROGRESSION\nEach Combat Style grants two foundational techniques whose requirements are intentionally low enough for a character choosing that style to use immediately. Each style also has three authored follow-on techniques at roughly seasoned, veteran and master skill bands. Prefer those existing abilities before inventing new combat techniques. The follow-ons are not class-locked: another character may learn them once their relevant skills, training, practice and story evidence make that credible. Do not grant the three follow-ons automatically at character creation.",
    "Sapphire Wake Magic Learning": "## RARE MAGIC\nTidecraft, Wake-Sight and Deep Calling still require established supernatural access through an Uncanny Gift, initiation, teacher, pact or story-earned opening. Salt Lore can be learned as scholarship without becoming spellcasting. Lower skill barriers do not make magic common. New magical techniques should extend the existing schools through teaching, proof or extraordinary contact; never invent generic spell lists, teleportation, effortless resurrection or reality editing.",
    "Sapphire Wake Naming and Scale": "## NAMES AND SCALE\nAbility names should sound like something a sailor, duelist, surgeon, hunter, navigator or court professional might actually call a practiced trick: short, concrete and rooted in deck, steel, gun, weather, chart, body, room or local tradition. Avoid numbered upgrades, generic MMO names and abstract machine-language metaphors. Nonmagical abilities stay physically possible and add a distinct permission, timing advantage or technique rather than a renamed skill check.",
    "Sapphire Wake Universal General Abilities": "## UNIVERSAL GENERAL TECHNIQUES\nAbilities with an empty `requirements` array are universal techniques. Any character may spend an Ability Point to learn one regardless of skill level, Calling, culture, faction or combat style. They represent broadly learnable habits such as keeping footing, taking stock, lending a hand, preserving an exit, passing a message or using an object already present. Their bonuses are intentionally modest and their descriptions are hard constraints: a universal technique never manufactures expertise, hidden information, authority, equipment, impossible movement or supernatural protection. Prefer these when a player wants useful breadth without first investing in a specialist skill.\n\nCHARACTER CREATION DISCIPLINE: Culture grants one cultural starter technique; Early Life one modest formative technique; each selected Calling one foundational professional technique; Faction Tie grants no ability; Uncanny Gift grants one entry-level supernatural technique; Combat Style grants two foundational fighting techniques. Do not restore removed advanced chargen grants merely because the character's biography sounds impressive. Advanced techniques belong to progression.",
    "Sapphire Wake Noncombat Ability Progression": "## NONCOMBAT TECHNIQUE PROGRESSION\nThe authored catalogue now includes deep maritime, exploration, investigation, social, romantic, command, commercial and legal techniques as well as combat and rare magic. Prefer these existing techniques when a character wants a named specialty instead of inventing a duplicate. A raw skill always remains usable without buying an ability; an ability represents a practiced method, timing advantage or distinct permission beyond ordinary competence.\n\nHybrid techniques require every listed skill and the physical/social conditions named in their descriptions. Leadership does not manufacture command authority; Law & Custom does not create jurisdiction; Navigation and Cartography do not reveal unseen geography; Stealth does not erase light, sound or access; social techniques do not compel choices. Seduction abilities can recognize, express and deepen genuinely reciprocal adult chemistry, but never create attraction, consent or intimacy from refusal."
  }
